WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W5 (0.0.4)


STATE

  Version 0.0.4, compound commands and functions, on branch dev. It
  completes Phase P1 (foundation) by adding:
  - compound commands: if/elif/else/fi, while, until, for (with and
    without 'in'), case (plain-string patterns plus exact bare '*'
    match-all; other unquoted globs refused until 0.1.0), { ...; } brace
    groups, ( ... ) subshells, and trailing redirections on any compound
    command (including inside pipelines);
  - shell functions (src/func.c: refcounted ASTs in private arenas,
    POSIX command lookup precedence, scoped positional parameters and
    prefix assignments, settable recursion limit via FUNCNEST defaulting
    to 1000 with hard ceiling 2000);
  - break, continue, and return special builtins with explicit flow
    state (no setjmp/longjmp);
  - explicit parser nesting limit (128), execution depth limit (8192),
    and arena mark/rewind for loop iterations.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass
  (289 unit checks, 80 script/refusal/startup checks against bash --posix).

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; unquoted expansions containing IFS characters pass
  through as a single word until field splitting lands in 0.1.0; case
  allows bare unquoted '*' as an exact match-all while refusing other
  unquoted globs until 0.1.0; FUNCNEST sets the function recursion limit.


NEXT

  1. 0.1.0, Phase P2 start (plans/P2-posix-language.md):
     - command substitution ($(...) and `...`);
     - $'...' ANSI-C quoting;
     - arithmetic expansion ($((...)));
     - IFS field splitting;
     - pathname expansion (globbing) with our own pattern matcher (also
       enabling full patterns in case and ${x%pat}/${x#pat}).
     Bump VERSION to 0.1.0 in the first code commit.

  2. 0.1.1, background commands, wait, trap, and the remaining special
     builtins (set, shift, eval, ., export, readonly, unset, exec, times).


